My healer found a throne room on DL14 and after the carnage
tested the throne in hopes of an ID more than anything. He
still was genoless, polyless and wishless (has a magic lamp,
holy water and a /oPoly) and content for the moment.

I choose my conducts to make the game more interesting or
fun rather than to demonstrate my expertise, so when a wish
popped up, I reflected on the fact that there were no
artifacts in my game so far. Was there anything I could wish
for that would make the game more interesting?

Well, I've never even seen the Eyes of the Overworld and
they sound like fun, why not. Then after about three more
tries at the throne, a second wish is offered. Well, how
about the Eye of the Aethiopica, it's fun zipping around the
dungeon and not having to conserve spell power!

The throne yielded a map of the level as well, it must have
last for 15 or 20 #sits!

I think to compensate for breaking the wishless conduct I'll
refrain from alchemy. Attempting to ascend without that
extra 160 HP will be a twist.
